        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 139 returns `audioLevel` in `RTCEncodedAudioFrame.getMetadata()`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27641</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27641"/>
        <updated>2025-08-22T18:18:09.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">…property</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 139 updates the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCEncodedAudioFrame/getMetadata" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">RTCEncodedAudioFrame.getMetadata()</code></a> method so that the <a href="https://w3c.github.io/webrtc-encoded-transform/#dom-rtcencodedaudioframemetadata-audiolevel" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">audioLevel</code></a> property is available in its return object. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5206106602995712" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5206106602995712</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a data point for the new return object property. The description might need a bit of work, as I wasn't sure of the standard for this kind of addition.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
