        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 139 adds `<button command="request-close">`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27628</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27628"/>
        <updated>2025-08-22T10:55:09.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 139 adds support for the <a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#attr-button-command-request-close" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">request-close</code></a> value of the <code class="notranslate">&lt;button&gt;</code> element's <code class="notranslate">command</code> attribute. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5592399713402880" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5592399713402880</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">BCD also includes a data point for the same value on the <code class="notranslate">HTMLButtonElement.command</code> DOM property.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds this data to the <code class="notranslate">&lt;button&gt;</code> element too, so it is available there.</p>

